    {
      "id": 264465,
      "name": "",
      "username": "LonelyMan",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2025-11-21T18:23:46.132Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I like that the names Z’ver and Com’Torr both evoke a considerable phonic similarity to Christopher.  Z’ver in particular is closer to C than to any other Terrestrially common name I can think of.  And it’s a character that specifically doesn’t want a bunch of humans calling him by a name that’s better for them because it’s not all alien sounding.</p>\n<p>True Tide isn’t a good name.  If not being on the nose with Black Tide, then definitely something more like Rising Tide.</p>\n<p>C&amp;A didn’t comment on it, but I really tremendously enjoyed how Zapdragon’s letter just slid in that comment about a Maerynian going “dry” with fear, where a human would have gone cold.</p>\n<p>Adam may not do much writing, but clearly he knows how to write Ray Manta.  That bit was pure gold.</p>\n<p>“the shark is more dorky than cool” - oh no, it’s Progeny’s head all over again!</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2025-11-21T19:42:17.379Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 8,
      "readers_count": 7,
      "score": 1.6,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 19938,
      "topic_slug": "episode-145-of-the-letters-page-writer-s-room-cosmic-tales-vol-2-issue-512",
      "display_username": "",
