      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 4,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "I like that the names Z'ver and Com'Torr both evoke a considerable phonic similarity to Christopher.  Z'ver in particular is closer to C than to any other Terrestrially common name I can think of.  And it's a character that specifically doesn't want a bunch of humans calling him by a name that's better for them because it's not all alien sounding.\n\nTrue Tide isn't a good name.  If not being on the nose with Black Tide, then definitely something more like Rising Tide.\n\nC&A didn't comment on it, but I really tremendously enjoyed how Zapdragon's letter just slid in that comment about a Maerynian going \"dry\" with fear, where a human would have gone cold.\n\nAdam may not do much writing, but clearly he knows how to write Ray Manta.  That bit was pure gold.\n\n\"the shark is more dorky than cool\" - oh no, it's Progeny's head all over again!",
